---
description: Enforce design token fidelity; ban arbitrary colors/spacing in UI work
alwaysApply: true
---

# Design Tokens

- Treat design tokens / CSS variables (or the Design System Architect handoff) as the source of truth for color, typography, spacing, radius, and elevation.
- Do not introduce one-off hex colors, arbitrary `px` padding/margins, or undocumented shadow values in UI components.
- If a new visual value is needed, add or request a token via Design System Architect first, then reference the token.
- Prefer semantic roles (e.g. `bg-surface`, `text-muted`, `border-danger`) over raw palette names in components.
- When reviewing UI diffs, reject changes that hardcode styles Design did not authorize.
